  "body": "Part of epic #1047. Design: hub-v2-v3-design-2026-10-26.md §6.\n\nThe hub can fail silently today: if the fleet feed goes stale or a section falls back to fixtures, the page still renders (the pm-feed pull-to-main caveat; collector boot-persistence is code#903, a dependency — do not duplicate it).\n\nAdd: (1) collector heartbeat timestamp carried in the feed; (2) aggregator surfaces feed age prominently (footer + /api/health) and flags any facet on fixture fallback; (3) a drift check on the sandbox pm-feed checkout vs origin/main, surfaced in the same health view; (4) stewardship's hourly staleness check (live in its DAILY CONSOLE READS block) names a stale feed as a finding.\nAcceptance: killing the collector in a test makes the dashboard visibly say so within one collector interval; silence means healthy.\n",
